From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: keep test sockets within sockaddr_un

The locked build path makes the longest generated test socket path 110
bytes, while Linux sockaddr_un.sun_path has room for 108 bytes including
the terminating null. Glibc fortification therefore aborts four tests at
server startup. Drop the redundant TEST_ prefix and use the current test
binary directory explicitly, keeping the longest path at 105 bytes without
skipping or weakening any test.

Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V package CI failure analysis
Patch-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes are not authorized)
---
 tests/CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/CMakeLists.txt b/tests/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/tests/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/tests/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ FUNCTION(addtest t)
             SRCDIR=${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}
             TNAME=${t}
             PATH=${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}:${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/tests:$ENV{PATH}
-            SEXPECT_SOCKFILE=${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/tests/TEST_${t}.sock
+            SEXPECT_SOCKFILE=${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/${t}.sock
     )
     set_tests_properties(
         ${t} PROPERTIES
